<Group view="presentation" inline-output="false" labelreference="L419" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">In order to validate numerically that the orbits do repeat and are periodic, I used the findpeaks in the Signal Processing toolbox to find local minima of my objective function. Findpeaks finds local maxima, so for the objective function I am minimizing to find the orbit, I just took the inverse. That objective function is the norm of each of the relative positional states minus the initial relative conditions. The algorithm for finding local mimimum of the objective function, which minimizes the total variance between the relative positional states and the relative positional initial conditions is shown below:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" inline-output="false" labelreference="L422" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
