</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" inline-output="false" labelreference="L428" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">First we are using the intial states and body vectors to create three relative vectors between each of the bodies. Next, the absolute value of the difference in the relative position versus the initial relative position is squared and the norm is taken for each of the components. This gave a numerical value for how close the initial conditions were. The assumption that the orbit is periodic is purely from the plotting of the graphics and the graphing of the objective function below:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
