<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The difference is the index of where the orbit periods occurs. Findpeaks is a good function, but can not individually grab the local minima that coincides with the orbit. The orbit period reaching closest to the initial conditions occurs around 0.3 indexes into the search, but there are other local minumum before it. That is why in the second to last line, the indmins has a 10 and 20. Those coincide with the local minimums at roughly 0.3 and 0.6. The first two absolute minima on the graph.</Text-field>
