<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">As expected in both cases, the three-bodies don't exactly match up with the relative initial conditions. The error increases in both cases as time goes on and the simulation increases, which is a function of error compounding in the ODE solver. I attempted as well to use the normal initial conditions, not the relative, but was not having success in implementing. This method, I believe is valid for finding the relative orbital period for the periodic orbits described. If there is another way to calculate the time period more fluidly, I would love to know. </Text-field>
